    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 2168,
      "versionNonce": 852790770,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "p4--2AXGfuLKMvkC_JIxy",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 956.332331735488,
      "y": -1838.6879335218891,
      "strokeColor": "#495057",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 1030.556822982054,
      "height": 972.5561671676644,
      "seed": 455767090,
      "groupIds": [
        "dbgITr1jDP9JB6H5lNMLs"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1763130775286,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 28.816479027190052,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "text": "Elliptic Curve (EC) Keys\n• IK = long-term Identity elliptic curve public Key\n• SPK = Signed elliptic curve prekey (medium-term, signed by IK)\n• OPK = One-time PreKey (single use)\n• EK = Ephemeral Key (generated per session)\n\nPost-Quantum Keys:\n• PQSPK = Signed last-resort Post-Quantum Key Encapsulation Mechanism\n(PQKEM) prekey. Signed with IK\n• (PQOPK1, PQOPK2, …) = Set of signed one-time pqkem prekeys. Signed with\nIK\n\nAlgorithms\n• EncodeEC() = A function that encodes a curve public key into a byte\nsequence\n• DecodeEC() = A function that decodes a byte sequence into a curve public\nkey and is the inverse of EncodeEC\n• EncodeKEM() = A function that encodes a pqkem public key into a byte\nsequence\n• DecodeKEM() = A function that decodes a byte sequence into a pqkem public\nkey and is the inverse of EncodeKEM\n• DH() = Elliptic Curve Diffie-Hellman function - combines a private key from\none party with a public key from another party to create a shared secret.\n• KDF() = Key Derivation Function (HKDF-SHA256) - takes \"raw\" key material\nand derives a cryptographically strong key from it.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Elliptic Curve (EC) Keys\n• IK = long-term Identity elliptic curve public Key\n• SPK = Signed elliptic curve prekey (medium-term, signed by IK)\n• OPK = One-time PreKey (single use)\n• EK = Ephemeral Key (generated per session)\n\nPost-Quantum Keys:\n• PQSPK = Signed last-resort Post-Quantum Key Encapsulation Mechanism (PQKEM) prekey. Signed with IK\n• (PQOPK1, PQOPK2, …) = Set of signed one-time pqkem prekeys. Signed with IK\n\nAlgorithms\n• EncodeEC() = A function that encodes a curve public key into a byte sequence\n• DecodeEC() = A function that decodes a byte sequence into a curve public key and is the inverse of EncodeEC\n• EncodeKEM() = A function that encodes a pqkem public key into a byte sequence\n• DecodeKEM() = A function that decodes a byte sequence into a pqkem public key and is the inverse of EncodeKEM\n• DH() = Elliptic Curve Diffie-Hellman function - combines a private key from one party with a public key from another party to create a shared secret.\n• KDF() = Key Derivation Function (HKDF-SHA256) - takes \"raw\" key material and derives a cryptographically strong key from it.",
      "lineHeight": 1.35,
      "baseline": 12,
      "index": "a4",
      "autoResize": false
    },
